1
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:20,601
The best revenge is to be beautiful.

2
00:00:20,601 --> 00:00:22,175
And the best place to be beautiful

3
00:00:22,175 --> 00:00:24,811
is at the Grand Gyronella University Ball.

4
00:00:24,811 --> 00:00:26,999
Don't experiment on me.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,531
But you're our friend, Florence.

6
00:00:29,531 --> 00:00:31,656
Friends help each other.

7
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:34,654
Friends are always there for each other.

8
00:00:34,654 --> 00:00:38,358
And friends party together!

9
00:00:38,358 --> 00:00:41,061
Friends always offer a helping hand.

10
00:00:41,061 --> 00:00:43,597
And when you get murdered,

11
00:00:43,597 --> 00:00:46,933
we, your friends, will avenge your death.

12
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:48,228
True.

13
00:00:49,369 --> 00:00:52,105
You're overreacting with the murder part.

14
00:00:52,105 --> 00:00:54,740
So, game?

15
00:00:56,990 --> 00:00:59,758
So, will you be my date?

16
00:01:02,549 --> 00:01:05,084
Don't you have any other choice?

17
00:01:05,717 --> 00:01:09,623
This is it, guys.
Welcome to this year's Grand Gyronella Ball.

18
00:01:09,623 --> 00:01:12,250
A celebration of humanity and beauty.

19
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:17,864
And it looks like the king and queen
have arrived.

20
00:01:17,864 --> 00:01:23,670
Here we have
Ms. Antonia Scarlet Vamorida Fuentes,

21
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:27,908
escorted by none other
than Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell.

22
00:01:27,908 --> 00:01:32,665
Antonia looks perfect in her sparkly,

23
00:01:32,665 --> 00:01:34,744
like-a-night-filled-with-stars dress.

24
00:01:34,744 --> 00:01:37,512
I think that's how I would be describing it.

25
00:01:42,055 --> 00:01:43,892
Florence?

26
00:01:43,892 --> 00:01:45,558
Can we just talk?

27
00:01:45,558 --> 00:01:46,860
No need.

28
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:48,762
I don't want people to see me.

29
00:01:48,762 --> 00:01:50,376
I look like a fool.

30
00:01:50,376 --> 00:01:52,376
Come on, Florence, it can't be that bad.

31
00:01:52,376 --> 00:01:54,601
Please, Owen, this is not me.

32
00:01:54,601 --> 00:01:57,570
You'll all laugh at me once you see me.

33
00:01:57,570 --> 00:01:59,472
I just want to see you and who knows,

34
00:01:59,472 --> 00:02:02,074
maybe Ma'am Serafica and I can help you.

35
00:02:08,101 --> 00:02:10,936
Okay, thank you for the update.

36
00:02:12,085 --> 00:02:13,753
What's happening?

37
00:02:13,753 --> 00:02:15,956
Is Florence okay?

38
00:02:15,956 --> 00:02:19,259
It seems she's not happy
with how she turned out earlier,

39
00:02:19,259 --> 00:02:22,877
that's why the stylist said
she might not come.

40
00:02:22,877 --> 00:02:24,299
Huh?

41
00:02:24,299 --> 00:02:27,167
It can't be that bad.

42
00:02:28,602 --> 00:02:30,756
Wow!

43
00:02:30,756 --> 00:02:34,006
That is crazy, bro!

44
00:02:35,728 --> 00:02:39,545
I'm not going to lie, they look good.

45
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:28,454
Don Ferell, Don Rogelio, excuse me.

46
00:03:28,454 --> 00:03:29,924
Yeah.

47
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:37,871
Grandpa.

48
00:03:37,871 --> 00:03:41,458
Owen, and of course
our beautiful Princess, Florence.

49
00:03:41,458 --> 00:03:44,009
Give your Grandpa Garp a kiss.

50
00:03:48,328 --> 00:03:51,523
It's nice to see you
in a different light, Florence.

51
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:55,459
And of course, your accessory is perfect.

52
00:04:02,008 --> 00:04:04,077
Hi, Florence.

53
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,278
Hello, Don Rogelio.

54
00:04:05,278 --> 00:04:08,882
I'm sorry I didn't notice that you were here.

55
00:04:08,882 --> 00:04:11,184
It was nice hanging out with you
the other day.

56
00:04:11,184 --> 00:04:12,919
Hanging out?

57
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:16,184
Yes, we saw each other
at Mr. Henry's chicken.

58
00:04:16,184 --> 00:04:18,792
That's one of Florence's favorite places.

59
00:04:18,792 --> 00:04:21,695
And I apologized to her about what happened.

60
00:04:21,695 --> 00:04:24,530
And somehow, we were able to talk.

61
00:04:25,792 --> 00:04:27,000
Yes, Grandpa Garp.

62
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,569
And Don Rogelio is also cool.

63
00:04:32,815 --> 00:04:37,444
And I envy you, Garpidio.
You found a great cook in her.

64
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:39,579
And from what I sense here,

65
00:04:39,579 --> 00:04:43,682
you bring a lot of positive energy
and happiness.

66
00:04:45,281 --> 00:04:49,718
She is special,
and I'm glad we got to know her.

67
00:04:51,310 --> 00:04:53,540
I'm sorry the music is on...

68
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:55,996
Owen, do you mind if I dance with Florence?

69
00:04:55,996 --> 00:04:58,164
Go ahead. Go ahead, sir.

70
00:05:23,223 --> 00:05:25,444
Do you like that guy, Owen?

71
00:05:25,444 --> 00:05:28,420
What? Owen?

72
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:32,053
We're just friends.

73
00:05:32,053 --> 00:05:36,323
When I look into your eyes, I see love.

74
00:05:48,915 --> 00:05:51,851
What makes you say that?

75
00:05:53,070 --> 00:05:55,439
I once fell in love...

76
00:05:56,276 --> 00:05:59,745
and I know it when I see it.

77
00:06:01,135 --> 00:06:04,964
What do I know about love?

78
00:06:04,964 --> 00:06:07,200
Love is complicated...

79
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,703
but if there's one advice I can give you,

80
00:06:09,703 --> 00:06:12,289
it is to listen to your heart

81
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:15,024
because your heart tells the truth.

82
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:24,117
Our heart is the reason
why we find people that we have lost,

83
00:06:24,117 --> 00:06:26,886
and have been separated from us
for a long time.

84
00:06:30,924 --> 00:06:34,093
You're really profound.

85
00:06:38,465 --> 00:06:40,069
Why is she there?

86
00:06:40,069 --> 00:06:41,267
Where did she get the money?

87
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:43,603
Federico, don't be like that.

88
00:06:43,603 --> 00:06:46,372
Let's call her tomorrow.
She will explain tomorrow.

89
00:06:46,372 --> 00:06:48,707
- No. Let's go.
- No, stop.

90
00:06:52,278 --> 00:06:54,613
I might trip.

91
00:07:04,844 --> 00:07:06,993
Another glass of wine, please.

92
00:07:06,993 --> 00:07:10,086
Antonia... that's enough.

93
00:07:11,297 --> 00:07:13,126
Why?

94
00:07:13,126 --> 00:07:16,392
Are you scared that I will make a scene here?

95
00:07:16,392 --> 00:07:19,227
Are you ashamed to be here with me?

96
00:07:20,573 --> 00:07:22,308
Antonia, please.

97
00:07:22,308 --> 00:07:26,045
I chose you,
that's why I won't leave your side.

98
00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:33,986
Let's stop fooling around here, Nero.

99
00:07:36,523 --> 00:07:41,294
You're here with me
because you have no choice.

100
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:43,763
Because even though you chose me,

101
00:07:43,763 --> 00:07:46,999
my heart wouldn't be hurting now.

102
00:08:00,495 --> 00:08:02,473
Fresh air?

103
00:08:02,473 --> 00:08:04,274
Yes.

104
00:08:05,552 --> 00:08:09,088
I'm sorry if I bothered you.

105
00:08:09,088 --> 00:08:11,292
It's fine.

106
00:08:11,292 --> 00:08:13,761
The space is huge.

107
00:08:13,761 --> 00:08:15,682
There's enough space for both of us.

108
00:08:15,682 --> 00:08:19,112
I'm just not used to places
with lots of people.

109
00:08:19,112 --> 00:08:22,101
Besides, I don't think
there's proper ventilation inside.

110
00:08:22,101 --> 00:08:25,004
We're probably breathing each other's breath.

111
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:26,872
Right!

112
00:08:28,328 --> 00:08:32,284
But I don't want to bother you anymore.

113
00:08:32,284 --> 00:08:34,128
I don't want to ruin your privacy.

114
00:08:34,128 --> 00:08:35,558
I'll leave you to it.

115
00:08:35,558 --> 00:08:37,449
Thank you.

116
00:08:43,310 --> 00:08:45,111
<i>Can I call?</i>

117
00:08:54,723 --> 00:08:57,491
Sorry, someone sent a message.

118
00:09:13,828 --> 00:09:15,855
<i>Sorry, you can't.</i>

119
00:09:15,855 --> 00:09:18,924
<i>I'm at an event
and there's a pest standing beside me.</i>

120
00:09:35,689 --> 00:09:40,432
<i>I'm also attending an event,
and there's a pest by my side.</i>

121
00:09:51,986 --> 00:09:55,268
<i>To be fair, my pest is dressed well.</i>

122
00:09:56,807 --> 00:09:59,631
<i>Really? What is the pest wearing?</i>

123
00:10:03,636 --> 00:10:07,573
<i>He is wearing a maroon and white suit.</i>

124
00:10:16,469 --> 00:10:21,008
<i>To be honest, the pest standing beside me
is cute in her dress.</i>

125
00:10:21,008 --> 00:10:24,923
<i>She's wearing a light green dress.</i>

126
00:11:00,005 --> 00:11:02,127
You're Ninja Copy Girl?

127
00:11:17,129 --> 00:11:19,090
Where is Lina?

128
00:11:20,043 --> 00:11:21,764
There she is.

129
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:24,617
Girl, where did you go?

130
00:11:24,617 --> 00:11:26,752
I just went out to get some fresh air.

131
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:32,262
Well, guess what,
we're now at the exciting part.

132
00:11:32,262 --> 00:11:35,098
Yes.

133
00:11:36,118 --> 00:11:37,845
What are you up to?

134
00:11:37,845 --> 00:11:40,706
What are you two planning?

135
00:11:40,706 --> 00:11:43,883
Just trust us girl, it will be fun.

136
00:11:43,883 --> 00:11:46,553
Exactly, as in super.

137
00:11:46,553 --> 00:11:48,188
Super.

138
00:11:48,188 --> 00:11:50,123
Maybe that's something foolish.

139
00:11:50,123 --> 00:11:52,057
Of course not.

140
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:56,362
Babycakes, come on!

141
00:11:56,362 --> 00:11:58,698
- No!
- Come on, Baby.

142
00:11:58,698 --> 00:12:00,033
No!

143
00:12:00,033 --> 00:12:01,850
You're such a killjoy.

144
00:12:01,850 --> 00:12:04,036
Come on, cheers.

145
00:12:06,306 --> 00:12:07,740
<i>Hello, hello!</i>

146
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:12,444
Good evening, Gyronella University!

147
00:12:15,137 --> 00:12:17,784
Oh my goodness, this is it.

148
00:12:17,784 --> 00:12:20,854
We're now here at the exciting part
of our Grand Ball.

149
00:12:20,854 --> 00:12:23,656
As if it couldn't get even grander.

150
00:12:23,656 --> 00:12:26,559
In fact, our theme is Return to Kindness,
right?

151
00:12:26,559 --> 00:12:29,562
And so, Ms. Camille Villarico and Aira Rivera

152
00:12:29,562 --> 00:12:34,834
thought of a way so we can raise more funds
and can help more people.

153
00:12:34,834 --> 00:12:38,671
And we call this,
Auction for the Greater Good.

154
00:12:40,773 --> 00:12:45,745
Well anyway, you might ask me,
how can we do this?

155
00:12:45,745 --> 00:12:48,781
So, we will present here an item or a prize,

156
00:12:48,781 --> 00:12:51,751
and of course,
everyone here has a chance to put on a bid.

157
00:12:51,751 --> 00:12:55,188
But of course, the highest bidder
will be winning that prize.

158
00:12:55,188 --> 00:12:58,150
So are you guys ready?
Are your wallets ready?

159
00:12:58,150 --> 00:13:01,394
- Yeah!
- Okay, seems like it.

160
00:13:01,394 --> 00:13:03,730
So, let's call on our first prize,

161
00:13:03,730 --> 00:13:07,900
or rather the first prize holder,
Mr. Tristan Ferell.

162
00:13:10,270 --> 00:13:12,935
Are you going to be auctioned? Just kidding.

163
00:13:12,935 --> 00:13:16,575
Anyway, what item do you have, Tristan?

164
00:13:18,511 --> 00:13:21,247
I have two tickets to a BTS Concert in Seoul.

165
00:13:21,247 --> 00:13:22,348
Oh my God.

166
00:13:22,348 --> 00:13:24,183
Who wants to go?

167
00:13:25,018 --> 00:13:26,319
Wow.

168
00:13:26,319 --> 00:13:28,054
I think a lot of people want to go with you.

169
00:13:28,054 --> 00:13:31,423
Let's go, Baby!

170
00:13:32,158 --> 00:13:33,726
Not now, maybe later.

171
00:13:33,726 --> 00:13:35,728
I'll think about it.

172
00:13:51,034 --> 00:13:54,603
So let's start the bidding,
let's get it rolling.

173
00:13:55,315 --> 00:13:56,723
Yes?

174
00:13:56,723 --> 00:13:58,184
20,000 pesos.

175
00:13:58,184 --> 00:14:02,355
20,000 immediately from the girl on Table 3!

176
00:14:02,355 --> 00:14:04,857
Do we hear a 30?

177
00:14:04,857 --> 00:14:06,893
30,000 pesos.

178
00:14:06,893 --> 00:14:07,894
Wow.

179
00:14:07,894 --> 00:14:13,099
30,000 from the girl on Table 5!

180
00:14:13,099 --> 00:14:15,301
Oh yes, Camille?

181
00:14:15,301 --> 00:14:19,772
Yes, 250,000 pesos.

182
00:14:19,772 --> 00:14:23,910
Wow, GU is just shocked right now.

183
00:14:23,910 --> 00:14:25,345
That's a big jump.

184
00:14:25,345 --> 00:14:27,680
Okay, that's 250,000 pesos

185
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:31,417
for two tickets to BTS Concert
with Mr. Tristan Ferell,

186
00:14:31,417 --> 00:14:35,120
sold to Ms. Camille Villarico!

187
00:14:37,023 --> 00:14:40,526
Lower! Lower! Lower!

188
00:14:40,526 --> 00:14:41,694
- Go, Baby!
- Lower!

189
00:14:41,694 --> 00:14:42,495
- Cakes!
- Lower!

190
00:14:42,495 --> 00:14:43,529
- Go, Baby!
- Lower!

191
00:14:43,529 --> 00:14:44,397
- Cakes!
- Lower!

192
00:14:44,397 --> 00:14:46,299
- Go, Baby!
- Cakes!

193
00:14:46,299 --> 00:14:48,301
- Go, Baby!
- Cakes!

194
00:14:48,301 --> 00:14:49,936
Go, Baby! Cakes!

195
00:14:49,936 --> 00:14:57,277
- Go, Baby!
- Cakes!

196
00:14:57,277 --> 00:14:59,078
Go, Baby!

197
00:15:25,207 --> 00:15:27,507
350,000 pesos!

198
00:15:27,507 --> 00:15:30,883
- Oh my God!
- Oh my God!

199
00:15:30,883 --> 00:15:36,528
If I'm not mistaken,
350,000 pesos from Ms. Aira Rivera.

200
00:15:36,528 --> 00:15:40,322
So, that famed Chef Jiro
will be cooking you dinner

201
00:15:40,322 --> 00:15:42,388
with Mr. Aldus Ferell.

202
00:15:42,388 --> 00:15:46,893
So oh, oh, congratulations!

203
00:15:46,893 --> 00:15:50,963
Wow, we're raising so many funds tonight, GU.

204
00:15:50,963 --> 00:15:52,552
So...

205
00:15:53,796 --> 00:15:55,764
what's your plan?

206
00:15:58,783 --> 00:16:00,650
I don't know too.

207
00:16:03,821 --> 00:16:06,125
Just tell her the truth.

208
00:16:10,838 --> 00:16:14,641
Do you think it's that easy?

209
00:16:19,058 --> 00:16:22,628
It looks like they're having fun in the ball.

210
00:16:22,628 --> 00:16:24,663
You can go back now.

211
00:16:27,123 --> 00:16:28,924
How about you?

212
00:16:30,069 --> 00:16:32,689
I already called my driver.

213
00:16:32,689 --> 00:16:34,907
I just want to go home.

214
00:16:34,907 --> 00:16:36,542
Are you sure?

215
00:16:36,542 --> 00:16:38,282
Why?

216
00:16:38,282 --> 00:16:41,071
Do you want me to change my mind?

217
00:16:41,071 --> 00:16:44,049
Because I'm only generous for a few minutes.

218
00:16:54,139 --> 00:16:55,912
Go back, Nero.

219
00:16:58,209 --> 00:16:59,420
Go to her.

220
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:01,319
Win her back.

221
00:17:01,319 --> 00:17:03,468
Win Florence back.

222
00:17:28,622 --> 00:17:31,466
So now, may I call on for our next item,

223
00:17:31,466 --> 00:17:34,132
Ms. Florence Dela Cruz?

224
00:17:36,736 --> 00:17:39,231
Yes, come on down.

225
00:17:39,231 --> 00:17:42,575
For this item, Florence will be
cooking you a private dinner

226
00:17:42,575 --> 00:17:44,617
in a set-up by the beach.

227
00:17:44,617 --> 00:17:49,549
So, Ms. Florence... Come join me.

228
00:17:49,549 --> 00:17:50,983
Go, Florence.

229
00:17:50,983 --> 00:17:53,519
You're being called on stage.

230
00:17:53,519 --> 00:17:55,775
- Come on, just go.
- Let's give Florence a round of applause.

231
00:17:55,775 --> 00:17:58,090
Go now.

232
00:18:02,161 --> 00:18:04,605
- A round of applause.
- Come on, just go.

233
00:18:04,605 --> 00:18:06,055
Go now.

234
00:18:10,564 --> 00:18:14,706
Ms. Dela Cruz, thanks for joining us.

235
00:18:16,017 --> 00:18:17,883
So, for everyone's information,

236
00:18:17,883 --> 00:18:21,554
Ms. Florence is the student representative
of the Com Arts Department.

237
00:18:21,554 --> 00:18:24,624
And they are responsible for
hosting our ball this evening.

238
00:18:24,624 --> 00:18:27,204
And she is also very sporting to participate

239
00:18:27,204 --> 00:18:30,256
in our Auction for the Greater Good,
so thank you.

240
00:18:30,256 --> 00:18:33,692
And of course, all funds raised
will be donated to charity.

241
00:18:33,692 --> 00:18:37,363
Ms. Florence, you know what?
I heard you're a very good cook.

242
00:18:37,363 --> 00:18:39,130
Is that right?

243
00:18:40,399 --> 00:18:45,245
I haven't poisoned anyone, so... I think yes?

244
00:18:47,873 --> 00:18:51,327
Sometimes,
I don't get the humor of poor people,

245
00:18:51,327 --> 00:18:54,480
but anyway, let's get this bidding started.

246
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,629
Private dinner cooked by Ms. Florence.

247
00:18:57,629 --> 00:18:59,184
Anyone?

248
00:18:59,184 --> 00:19:01,553
50,000 pesos.

249
00:19:01,553 --> 00:19:03,989
Babycakes, who is that guy?

250
00:19:03,989 --> 00:19:05,958
I have no idea.

251
00:19:05,958 --> 00:19:09,728
In fairness with Ms. Florence,
she's a box office hit.

252
00:19:09,728 --> 00:19:13,299
Yes, a lot of people are bidding.

253
00:19:13,299 --> 00:19:20,505
Maybe that's because
Florence brings the hope of love.

254
00:19:21,707 --> 00:19:26,211
And whoever sees her beauty,

255
00:19:26,211 --> 00:19:31,483
will overcome everything just to achieve it.

256
00:19:31,483 --> 00:19:32,518
He's wasted.

257
00:19:32,518 --> 00:19:34,326
He's already drunk.

258
00:19:34,326 --> 00:19:36,288
- I support her.
- Quiet, all of you!

259
00:19:36,288 --> 00:19:38,057
This is the continuation of the story.

260
00:19:38,057 --> 00:19:40,058
Can you please...

261
00:19:42,361 --> 00:19:43,978
Beautiful.

262
00:19:45,564 --> 00:19:47,866
- Anyone?
- Florence!

263
00:19:47,866 --> 00:19:50,001
One million pesos.

264
00:19:52,438 --> 00:19:57,042
One million p-pesos?

265
00:19:57,042 --> 00:20:00,179
That's a lot of feeding programs,
in that case.

266
00:20:00,179 --> 00:20:01,914
So, anyone?

267
00:20:01,914 --> 00:20:05,050
And if any of you are planning to outbid me,

268
00:20:05,050 --> 00:20:07,419
don't try anymore.

269
00:20:07,419 --> 00:20:10,289
Because I won't waste this chance

270
00:20:10,289 --> 00:20:13,291
to be with an important person to me.

271
00:20:13,926 --> 00:20:17,910
I won't waste the chance
to be with you again, Florence.

272
00:20:36,085 --> 00:20:37,819
Florence!

273
00:20:40,386 --> 00:20:42,755
Florence, wait!

274
00:20:42,755 --> 00:20:43,756
Florence!

275
00:20:43,756 --> 00:20:45,357
Florence, wait!

276
00:20:45,357 --> 00:20:49,928
Nero, please, leave me alone.

277
00:20:49,928 --> 00:20:51,842
Okay, but it's cold here...

278
00:20:51,842 --> 00:20:54,499
What are you doing?

279
00:20:57,736 --> 00:20:59,671
Are you playing a prank on me, Nero?

280
00:20:59,671 --> 00:21:03,208
Are you playing with me?
What do you think of me, a doll?

281
00:21:03,208 --> 00:21:04,877
Your toy car?

282
00:21:04,877 --> 00:21:07,478
- No.
- No?

283
00:21:09,148 --> 00:21:13,285
And what went into your mind earlier?
Why did you make a bid?

284
00:21:13,285 --> 00:21:17,488
Didn't you even think how Antonia would feel?

285
00:21:18,223 --> 00:21:20,659
Antonia and I are over.

286
00:21:20,659 --> 00:21:24,897
So you called it quits again,
so now, you're going after me?

287
00:21:24,897 --> 00:21:29,301
What?
You'll use me again to make her jealous?

288
00:21:29,301 --> 00:21:30,936
That's it?

289
00:21:30,936 --> 00:21:34,572
Have you forgotten what you told me?

290
00:21:35,641 --> 00:21:37,442
I'm sorry.

291
00:21:38,408 --> 00:21:40,176
Sorry?

292
00:21:42,614 --> 00:21:45,217
Nero, I don't want this anymore.

293
00:21:45,217 --> 00:21:49,220
I don't want to expect. I don't want to hope.

294
00:21:50,197 --> 00:21:55,124
I don't want to open my heart to you,
because it hurts.

295
00:21:55,124 --> 00:22:00,170
It hurts when you make a mistake
and believe that it's for real.

296
00:22:01,729 --> 00:22:03,697
So, please...

297
00:22:04,811 --> 00:22:07,846
Don't play with my heart.

298
00:22:11,510 --> 00:22:13,344
I'm sorry.

299
00:22:27,694 --> 00:22:31,296
Florence? What happened?

300
00:22:31,296 --> 00:22:32,564
Is there a problem?

301
00:22:32,564 --> 00:22:34,332
Grandfather...

302
00:22:43,881 --> 00:22:45,782
Stop crying, my grandchild.

303
00:22:56,595 --> 00:22:58,290
Dude, you have to relax.

304
00:22:58,290 --> 00:22:59,525
Grandfather is mad.

305
00:22:59,525 --> 00:23:02,047
Florence is missing,
so don't add to his problem.

306
00:23:02,047 --> 00:23:03,248
It's Nero's fault.

307
00:23:03,248 --> 00:23:05,517
He's acting as if he controls everything.

308
00:23:05,517 --> 00:23:07,486
Are you mad at Nero because he's being Nero?

309
00:23:07,486 --> 00:23:10,421
Or you're mad at him
because Florence likes him?

310
00:23:12,424 --> 00:23:15,928
Look, dude... it's too complicated.

311
00:23:15,928 --> 00:23:20,065
If I'm being honest,
you should both stop pursuing Florence.

312
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:23,669
It's you who said that Florence is our cook,

313
00:23:23,669 --> 00:23:27,972
and it's not good to see
that both Ferells are fighting because of her.

314
00:23:28,807 --> 00:23:31,510
That's the problem with both of you.

315
00:23:31,510 --> 00:23:34,879
You don't care about
how each other would feel.

316
00:23:36,014 --> 00:23:38,584
Sit together and talk.

317
00:23:38,584 --> 00:23:41,819
Man-to-man, from one Ferell to another.

318
00:23:49,361 --> 00:23:52,249
Imagine, what would people think
if they find out

319
00:23:52,249 --> 00:23:55,167
that you and Owen are fighting over her?

320
00:23:55,167 --> 00:23:57,636
I don't care what others would say.

321
00:23:57,636 --> 00:24:00,439
My God, dude, you're both Ferells.

322
00:24:00,439 --> 00:24:02,808
Have you forgotten what Grandfather said?

323
00:24:02,808 --> 00:24:07,946
That if we, Ferells, have a problem,
we fix it, together.

324
00:24:07,946 --> 00:24:10,816
That's right. Just fix that problem.

325
00:24:10,816 --> 00:24:13,386
The last thing we want
is us to tearing each other apart

326
00:24:13,386 --> 00:24:15,720
because of Florence.

327
00:24:19,210 --> 00:24:20,425
Hello, Serafica.

328
00:24:20,425 --> 00:24:22,828
Is Florence there?

329
00:24:22,828 --> 00:24:24,329
She's not back yet, Don Ferell.

330
00:24:24,329 --> 00:24:26,331
But the boys are here already.

331
00:24:26,331 --> 00:24:29,534
Call me once Florence is back.

332
00:24:43,737 --> 00:24:46,251
Are you sure about this?

333
00:24:46,251 --> 00:24:48,554
If Florence did walk home,

334
00:24:48,554 --> 00:24:52,357
this is the nearest route
going back to the mansion.

335
00:24:52,357 --> 00:24:54,026
But Don Ferell,

336
00:24:54,026 --> 00:24:57,596
we've been driving around
for quite some time.

337
00:24:57,596 --> 00:25:03,168
Why don't we call her parents,
Lydia and Federico?

338
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:06,004
Maybe she went home to them.

339
00:25:12,611 --> 00:25:13,879
Hello?

340
00:25:13,879 --> 00:25:15,646
<i>Garpidio.</i>

341
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:25,357
Rogelio, we have an emergency here.

342
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:27,693
Can we just talk tomorrow?

343
00:25:27,693 --> 00:25:30,503
Is this about your cook named Florence?

344
00:25:32,898 --> 00:25:36,468
You don't have to worry. Florence is here.

345
00:25:36,468 --> 00:25:38,870
<i>The kid will spend the night here.</i>

346
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:42,007
<i>But don't worry, she's safe here.</i>

347
00:25:42,007 --> 00:25:44,458
She was crying earlier.

348
00:25:45,410 --> 00:25:49,548
<i>She's probably safe here...</i>

349
00:25:49,548 --> 00:25:50,716
away from your grandsons,

350
00:25:50,716 --> 00:25:55,087
whose relationship is a bit complicated
with her.

351
00:25:55,087 --> 00:25:56,922
I'll talk to you tomorrow.

352
00:25:56,922 --> 00:25:58,956
Goodnight, Garpidio.

353
00:26:09,368 --> 00:26:11,702
Let's go home, Dencio.

354
00:26:13,517 --> 00:26:15,318
Okay.

355
00:28:16,695 --> 00:28:20,064
The wealth of the Almeros is something else.

356
00:28:36,415 --> 00:28:39,016
I wonder where Grandfather Roger is?

357
00:29:07,549 --> 00:29:09,551
She's my daughter-in-law.

358
00:29:10,927 --> 00:29:12,728
Her name's Alyanna.

359
00:29:17,856 --> 00:29:19,558
Are you okay, Florence?

360
00:29:19,558 --> 00:29:22,093
Yes. I'm doing okay.

361
00:29:23,328 --> 00:29:25,697
Let's have breakfast.
I'm sure you're hungry now.

362
00:29:25,697 --> 00:29:27,032
No, thank you.

363
00:29:27,032 --> 00:29:29,634
I'll go ahead first, Grandfather Roger.

364
00:29:29,634 --> 00:29:30,844
Are you sure?

365
00:29:30,844 --> 00:29:34,272
Yes, and I'm so embarrassed,
I've caused you so much trouble.

366
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:37,576
And I'm also thinking about Grandfather Garp.

367
00:29:37,576 --> 00:29:40,278
- I'll ask the driver to take you home.
- No need.

368
00:29:40,278 --> 00:29:42,681
You've done so much for me.

369
00:29:42,681 --> 00:29:45,383
I'll just take the tricycle home.

370
00:29:46,518 --> 00:29:47,853
All right.

371
00:29:47,853 --> 00:29:51,022
Well, if there's anything you need...

372
00:29:51,022 --> 00:29:55,660
you are welcome in this house, Florence.

373
00:29:55,660 --> 00:30:00,164
Thank you, Grandfather Roger.
It was nice meeting you.

374
00:30:06,304 --> 00:30:09,541
Good Morning, Gyronella University.

375
00:30:09,541 --> 00:30:12,777
And we are back to regular programming.

376
00:30:12,777 --> 00:30:16,915
After the Grand GU Ball last night,

377
00:30:16,915 --> 00:30:18,917
it's officially the morning after,

378
00:30:18,917 --> 00:30:21,686
and I know a lot of my followers out there

379
00:30:21,686 --> 00:30:25,624
are excited to know
the highlights from last night.

380
00:30:25,624 --> 00:30:27,993
That's because a lot of things happened,

381
00:30:27,993 --> 00:30:32,230
like, a lot of people were trying
to outshine others.

382
00:30:32,230 --> 00:30:35,033
A lot of people took it to the next level.

383
00:30:35,033 --> 00:30:39,704
And actually, I think there was fighting too.

384
00:30:39,704 --> 00:30:44,105
And we also would want to know
who was the standout, and...

385
00:30:44,105 --> 00:30:48,813
well, let's just say,
those who slightly made a mark.

386
00:30:48,813 --> 00:30:51,683
But before we proceed to our rundown,

387
00:30:51,683 --> 00:30:54,419
let me welcome our special guest for today.

388
00:30:54,419 --> 00:30:58,690
And to be honest,
I didn't expect to see this person

389
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:01,059
at the Grand GU Ball last night.

390
00:31:01,059 --> 00:31:05,630
Let us all welcome, Aristotle Rah Cortez.

391
00:31:05,630 --> 00:31:09,801
Hello, Ash.
And hello to the listeners of GU TV.

392
00:31:09,801 --> 00:31:11,770
- Thanks, Aristotle.
- Of course.

393
00:31:11,770 --> 00:31:15,540
And you know,
you coming to the Grand GU Ball last night

394
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:20,211
is like one of the highlights
of our evening, right?

395
00:31:20,211 --> 00:31:22,881
And I just want to know,

396
00:31:22,881 --> 00:31:26,084
how did you get to the Grand GU Ball,

397
00:31:26,084 --> 00:31:30,722
considering that you come
from the rival university,

398
00:31:30,722 --> 00:31:33,325
which is Denison University.

399
00:31:33,325 --> 00:31:37,429
Well, to be honest, even with us in Denison,

400
00:31:37,429 --> 00:31:41,099
we look forward to
the Grand Ball of Gyronella.

401
00:31:41,099 --> 00:31:43,401
But in all honesty,

402
00:31:43,401 --> 00:31:47,906
we always felt like the event
is a bit excessive.

403
00:31:47,906 --> 00:31:50,875
Symptomatic of what is wrong in our country.

404
00:31:50,875 --> 00:31:54,946
Imagine, real people,
I mean rich people partying,

405
00:31:54,946 --> 00:31:58,183
unmindful of the things
happening in our country.

406
00:31:58,183 --> 00:32:00,652
But last night, my eyes were open,

407
00:32:00,652 --> 00:32:07,759
and it's not just about rich kids partying.

408
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:10,328
Because last night was also
about raising funds,

409
00:32:10,328 --> 00:32:14,999
so there's something you can give
the underserved communities.

410
00:32:15,667 --> 00:32:18,269
I will be honest, I am truly impressed.

411
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:22,407
And I'm starting to think
that Gyronella is the better school.

412
00:32:22,407 --> 00:32:23,875
Well, to be fair,

413
00:32:23,875 --> 00:32:26,478
it wasn't always like this in our university,

414
00:32:26,478 --> 00:32:29,214
but thank you to the efforts
of our new student

415
00:32:29,214 --> 00:32:32,350
and the representative
of Com Arts Department,

416
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:34,852
Ms. Florence Dela Cruz.

417
00:33:37,464 --> 00:33:39,298
Grandfather Garp?

418
00:33:49,394 --> 00:33:51,729
Florence is back, guys.

419
00:33:54,799 --> 00:33:57,235
You got us worried.

420
00:33:57,235 --> 00:34:00,671
Yeah. Did you enjoy your night out?

421
00:34:01,639 --> 00:34:03,575
Night out?

422
00:34:03,575 --> 00:34:04,843
Maybe I just got tired,

423
00:34:04,843 --> 00:34:08,713
that's why I fell asleep
in the Almero's mansion.

424
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:10,849
Are you okay?

425
00:34:10,849 --> 00:34:13,651
Yeah, I'm okay.

426
00:34:13,651 --> 00:34:17,455
By the way,
can you please return this to Camille?

427
00:34:17,455 --> 00:34:20,091
It's so expensive, I might lose and ruin it.

428
00:34:20,091 --> 00:34:21,126
I'll take care of it.

429
00:34:21,126 --> 00:34:23,427
Thank you. You're the best.

430
00:34:24,229 --> 00:34:28,599
Don Ferell, here are the people
you called for.

431
00:34:50,388 --> 00:34:51,689
You didn't tell us

432
00:34:51,689 --> 00:34:54,225
that the people you're cooking for
are young men.

433
00:34:54,225 --> 00:34:57,773
All this while, I thought Don Ferell's
grandsons are kindergarteners.

434
00:34:58,563 --> 00:35:02,066
But Don Ferell already explained to us

435
00:35:02,066 --> 00:35:05,436
your situation with Nero and Owen.

436
00:35:05,436 --> 00:35:09,661
Florence, it's not a good situation.

437
00:35:09,661 --> 00:35:12,409
That's why your father and I have decided

438
00:35:12,409 --> 00:35:16,314
that you'll stop cooking for this household.

439
00:35:16,314 --> 00:35:19,918
But, Mother, it's a pity if I let go of the...

440
00:35:19,918 --> 00:35:22,786
What? You're thinking about the salary?

441
00:35:25,256 --> 00:35:28,042
Do you think I'd be at peace

442
00:35:28,042 --> 00:35:31,462
knowing that you're cooking
for young men who are falling for you?

443
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:35,333
But we're still thankful to Don Ferell,

444
00:35:35,333 --> 00:35:38,942
because he said he'll continue
giving you a scholarship.

445
00:35:38,942 --> 00:35:40,438
As for the extra income,

446
00:35:40,438 --> 00:35:43,975
don't worry about that Florence,
because we have found a new job.

447
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:47,245
There's a caterer who'll hire us
as a regular staff

448
00:35:47,245 --> 00:35:49,814
to make their pastries.

449
00:35:49,814 --> 00:35:54,752
That's enough for your father's medication
and your schooling.

450
00:35:54,752 --> 00:35:58,223
And perfect timing because
it's your semester break.

451
00:35:58,223 --> 00:36:01,958
We'll be able to save up
for your next semester.

452
00:36:04,262 --> 00:36:07,565
I understand, Father.

453
00:36:07,565 --> 00:36:08,936
I'm sorry.

454
00:36:11,311 --> 00:36:14,505
Come on, pack your things.

455
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:16,129
We're leaving.

456
00:36:20,378 --> 00:36:22,814
Just understand your father.

457
00:36:22,814 --> 00:36:25,015
He's just worried about you.

458
00:36:30,492 --> 00:36:32,151
I'm sorry, Mother.

459
00:36:33,558 --> 00:36:35,097
Let's go.

460
00:36:46,271 --> 00:36:49,489
Girls, look at this.

461
00:36:49,489 --> 00:36:56,281
South Korean trip booking
is confirmed, right?

462
00:36:56,281 --> 00:37:01,119
Tristan, I am so excited
for our South Korean trip.

463
00:37:01,119 --> 00:37:05,122
Annyeong haseyo. Kamsa hamnida.

464
00:37:06,591 --> 00:37:10,361
Let me remind you, Camille, it's not a date.

465
00:37:10,361 --> 00:37:12,563
We'll go there to watch BTS,

466
00:37:12,563 --> 00:37:15,967
and I'll be there
to appreciate Jung Kook's greatness.

467
00:37:15,967 --> 00:37:18,269
Of course, me too.

468
00:37:18,269 --> 00:37:20,571
I'm definitely there for the music.

469
00:37:20,571 --> 00:37:23,107
If you want extracurricular activities,

470
00:37:23,107 --> 00:37:25,910
I'm willing and able.

471
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:28,346
Curricular?

472
00:37:28,346 --> 00:37:29,814
Yeah, you know,

473
00:37:29,814 --> 00:37:33,685
cultural immersion
and a tour of the Gyeongbokgung palace,

474
00:37:33,685 --> 00:37:35,086
something like that.

475
00:37:35,086 --> 00:37:36,654
How about you, Aldus?

476
00:37:36,654 --> 00:37:38,790
Have you packed already
for our trip to Japan?

477
00:37:38,790 --> 00:37:40,341
Yeah.

478
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:42,860
And aside from our date with Chef Jiro,

479
00:37:42,860 --> 00:37:44,462
do you have other plans?

480
00:37:44,462 --> 00:37:46,264
First, it's not a date.

481
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:48,433
What you won in the auction
is a treat from me

482
00:37:48,433 --> 00:37:50,902
to eat from the best sushi chef in the world.

483
00:37:50,902 --> 00:37:53,938
And second,
after our dinner date with Chef Jiro,

484
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:55,940
we're on our own in Tokyo.

485
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:57,908
You're such a snob.

486
00:37:58,876 --> 00:38:00,244
How about you, Lina?

487
00:38:00,244 --> 00:38:02,347
What's your plan for this academic break?

488
00:38:02,347 --> 00:38:03,881
Me?

489
00:38:03,881 --> 00:38:05,116
I'll just stay at home.

490
00:38:05,116 --> 00:38:08,086
Maybe the truth is
you'll be flirting with Troy.

491
00:38:08,086 --> 00:38:10,788
- Of course not.
- No, no, no.

492
00:38:10,788 --> 00:38:12,724
Why are you both defensive?

493
00:38:12,724 --> 00:38:13,791
True.

494
00:38:13,791 --> 00:38:15,026
And we all know,

495
00:38:15,026 --> 00:38:17,662
you guys are both
negativity-charged particles.

496
00:38:17,662 --> 00:38:22,766
And if Newton is correct,
you will always repel each other.

497
00:38:24,502 --> 00:38:28,172
And why does it seem like
the Ferells are hot-tempered?

498
00:38:28,172 --> 00:38:33,578
Yes, if they're not hot-tempered,
they're moody.

499
00:38:33,578 --> 00:38:36,380
Is there a problem at home?

500
00:38:41,819 --> 00:38:44,622
Troy, Tristan, and Aldus

501
00:38:44,622 --> 00:38:48,659
are discreetly exchanging
knowing looks with each other.

502
00:38:48,659 --> 00:38:51,562
It seems they're hiding something.

503
00:38:53,498 --> 00:38:55,633
Looks like there's a problem at home.

504
00:38:55,633 --> 00:38:57,068
It's Florence.

505
00:38:57,068 --> 00:38:59,771
To some extent, also Owen.

506
00:38:59,771 --> 00:39:01,472
Why? What happened?

507
00:39:01,472 --> 00:39:03,307
Florence is gone.

508
00:39:03,307 --> 00:39:06,677
She resigned as the cook in the mansion.

509
00:39:07,705 --> 00:39:09,399
What?

510
00:39:14,118 --> 00:39:17,054
We will miss you so much.

511
00:39:21,159 --> 00:39:22,993
Mr. Dencio...

512
00:39:24,862 --> 00:39:27,130
are you crying?

513
00:39:28,466 --> 00:39:30,334
Don't cry.

514
00:39:30,334 --> 00:39:32,136
You can visit me.

515
00:39:32,136 --> 00:39:35,473
Bring all of them during your day off.

516
00:39:35,473 --> 00:39:37,675
Me, crying?

517
00:39:37,675 --> 00:39:40,644
I'm not a crybaby.

518
00:39:42,346 --> 00:39:46,102
Be patient with Dencio, he cries easily.

519
00:39:46,102 --> 00:39:50,855
Yesterday, he kept on crying
because the sunshine is beautiful.

520
00:39:50,855 --> 00:39:53,457
It was really beautiful.

521
00:39:54,988 --> 00:39:57,223
Mr. Dencio, you're something else.

522
00:39:59,997 --> 00:40:03,701
I'll treasure the times
I was here in the mansion

523
00:40:03,701 --> 00:40:05,602
with all of you.

524
00:40:06,270 --> 00:40:09,340
In the short time we were together,

525
00:40:09,340 --> 00:40:12,510
I learned a lot of things from all of you.

526
00:40:12,510 --> 00:40:17,714
And I became a better person
because I met all of you.

527
00:40:22,453 --> 00:40:25,056
Stop. Please go.

528
00:40:25,056 --> 00:40:28,439
You'll really make us all cry.

529
00:40:28,439 --> 00:40:30,047
Go ahead.

530
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:34,831
Let's do a group hug first.

531
00:40:53,731 --> 00:40:55,381
Bye.

532
00:40:56,158 --> 00:40:58,068
You take care, okay?

533
00:41:15,426 --> 00:41:18,588
So do you think Nero
will try to win her back?

534
00:41:18,588 --> 00:41:20,611
This is exciting.

535
00:41:20,611 --> 00:41:22,146
I hope they patch things up,

536
00:41:22,146 --> 00:41:24,482
and I hope they'll end up together.

537
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:26,417
So there'll be a sequel to this story.

538
00:41:26,417 --> 00:41:29,019
When I thought
that letting go would be difficult,

539
00:41:29,019 --> 00:41:33,090
but the truth is,
I seem to be coping pretty well.

540
00:41:33,090 --> 00:41:34,091
That's good.

541
00:41:34,091 --> 00:41:36,961
You act like I'm the only broken-hearted one.

542
00:41:36,961 --> 00:41:38,603
What about you?

543
00:41:39,494 --> 00:41:41,632
I can't believe that girl.

544
00:41:41,632 --> 00:41:45,503
The audacity to show herself to us
after what she did to Florence.

545
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:48,606
She's using her charms again to trap Owen.

546
00:41:48,606 --> 00:41:52,209
Lina, why don't you keep an eye on Owen?

547
00:41:52,209 --> 00:41:55,402
I think you two will be perfect together.

548
00:41:55,402 --> 00:41:57,515
Yes.

549
00:41:57,515 --> 00:41:59,016
Good morning, Mother!

550
00:41:59,016 --> 00:42:01,418
Good morning, Father!

551
00:42:04,955 --> 00:42:06,757
Good Morning, Florence.

552
00:42:06,757 --> 00:42:09,123
What are you doing here?

553
00:42:09,123 --> 00:42:13,097
Florence, he's been waiting here
for quite some time.

554
00:42:13,097 --> 00:42:16,066
He said you owe him a dinner,

555
00:42:16,066 --> 00:42:20,738
because in the auction,
he bid one million for you to cook for him.

556
00:42:20,738 --> 00:42:22,240
Is that true?
